    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I reproduced this on latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nSee here:\n\nhttps://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/blob/261918f939a7262b7600b6fe117e46612dc4c62f/configs/nvim-0.11/plugin/20_keymaps.lua#L150\n\nAs far as I can tell the picker doesn't exist anywhere else (though could be defined by the user, of course).\n\n### Reproduction\n\n- Start nvim with a fresh config\n- Type ` fp` (`<leader>fp`)\n- See:\n  ```\n  Error executing Lua callback: (mini.pick) There is no picker named \"projects\" in registry.\n  stack traceback:\n          [C]: in function 'error'\n          ...re/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/pick.lua:3496: in function 'error'\n          ...re/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/pick.lua:2039: in function <...re/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/pick.lua:2036>\n  ```\n",
